Goal:
Visualize 2 pipelines (Champion and Challenger) processing the same requests through 8 nodes and compare pass vs fail counts at every node.

Tech stack:
- React 19
- TypeScript
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui
- Framer Motion
- Lucide React

Theme:
- Background: #020617
- Cards: #0F172A
- Borders: #1E293B
- Text: #E2E8F0
- Muted: #94A3B8
- Champion color: #22C55E
- Challenger color: #3B82F6
- Fail color: #EF4444

Layout:
- Full-screen responsive dashboard
- Top header
- Center comparison pipeline
- Right summary panel
- Glassmorphism cards
- Rounded 20px
- Subtle shadows and gradients

Header:
- Title: Champion vs Challenger – Funnel Pipeline
- Subtitle: 10 Requests each
- Right side: View Mode dropdown (Counts / Percentage)

Main content:
Use a 4-column layout:

LEFT COLUMN (Champion)
- Label card: CHAMPION / 10 Total
- 8 horizontal progress bars stacked vertically
- Each bar shows pass count in green and fail count in red
- Animate widths on load

CENTER COLUMN (Nodes)
Create 8 connected node cards vertically:

1. Device Trust
2. Velocity Check
3. IP / Location Risk
4. User Behavior
5. Device Fingerprint
6. Transaction Pattern
7. Risk Score Check
8. Final Decision

Each node card:
- 56px icon circle
- Node number
- Node title
- Node type (Rule Node / ML Node / Decision Node)
- Border glow on hover
- Connector lines between nodes

RIGHT COLUMN (Challenger)
- Label card: CHALLENGER / 10 Total
- 8 horizontal progress bars stacked vertically
- Pass in blue, fail in red
- Animate widths on load

FAR RIGHT COLUMN (Summary)
Create a sticky summary card showing:

Total Requests
- Champion: 10
- Challenger: 10

Approved
- Champion: 6 (60%)
- Challenger: 1 (10%)

Dropped
- Champion: 1 (10%)
- Challenger: 0 (0%)

Pass Rate
- Champion: 90%
- Challenger: 70%

Drop Rate
- Champion: 10%
- Challenger: 0%

Use green for better values and red for worse values.

